{"items":[{"item":{"id":"customer-references#collaboration-ai-second-front-chainguard-2025","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"collaboration-ai-second-front-chainguard-2025","dateCreated":"2025-02-17T19:46:43+0000","dateUpdated":"2025-02-19T21:17:52+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"\u003cp\u003eCollaboration.Ai, a leader in AI-driven innovation management software, sought to expand into the US federal government sector, particularly the Department of Defense (DoD), with its end-to-end CrowdVector innovation management platform. Obtaining the required Authority to Operate (ATO) on DoD networks\u0026mdash;a complex, lengthy, and costly process\u0026mdash;posed a significant challenge for the startup. By engaging with AWS Partner Second Front, a member of the AWS Global Security \u0026amp; Compliance Acceleration (GSCA) program and using its Game Warden DevSecOps platform on AWS GovCloud (US), Collaboration.Ai secured a Certificate to Field (CTF) for DoD networks in less than 90 days. The deployment was accelerated further by using a custom registry of secure, minimal container images from AWS Partner Chainguard. This approach saved nearly two years of work and $2 million in compliance costs, swiftly opening access to the US federal government market.\u003c/p\u003e\n","featured":"0","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/partner-network/partner_marketing_web_team/directories-logos/Collaboration.Ai_Logo_1__300x50.14548e71e4ebec3d66e21b1a104c6cebe41d8989.png","displayLocation":"United States","footerInfoText":"2025","industry":"Software \u0026 Internet","sortDate":"2025-02-17","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/collaboration.ai-second-front-chainguard/","customer-name":"Collaboration.Ai","enableShare":"1","publishedDate":"2025","contentType":"Case Study","headline":"Collaboration.Ai Achieves DoD Authorization in Less Than 90 Days, Saves $2 Million with Second Front, Chainguard, and AWS"}},"tags":[{"id":"GLOBAL#location#namer","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"North America","description":"North America","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:03+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#elb","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","description":"Elastic Load Balancing (ELB)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:03:09+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#industry#software-internet","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#industry","name":"Software \u0026 Internet","description":"Software \u0026 Internet","dateCreated":"2020-06-25T04:08:24+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:09+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#efs","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)","description":"Amazon Elastic File System (EFS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:57+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:32+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#eks","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)","description":"Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (EKS)","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:58+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:32+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#content-type#case-study","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#content-type","name":"Case Study","description":"Case Study","dateCreated":"2020-04-29T05:19:20+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:07+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#language#english","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#language","name":"English","description":"English","dateCreated":"2020-03-03T06:40:42+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:23+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#tech-category#security-identity-compliance","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#tech-category","name":"Security, Identity, \u0026 Compliance","description":"Security, Identity, \u0026 Compliance","dateCreated":"2020-01-16T17:43:33+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:35:33+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#location#united-states","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#location","name":"United States","description":"United States","dateCreated":"2020-02-03T05:29:08+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:31:34+0000"},{"id":"GLOBAL#product#ec2","locale":"en_US","tagNamespaceId":"GLOBAL#product","name":"Amazon EC2","description":"Amazon EC2","dateCreated":"2020-03-02T07:02:51+0000","dateUpdated":"2022-02-03T03:32:31+0000"}]},{"item":{"id":"customer-references#mazzuma","locale":"en_US","directoryId":"customer-references","name":"mazzuma","dateCreated":"2024-09-23T23:20:16+0000","dateUpdated":"2024-09-23T23:21:13+0000","additionalFields":{"descriptionSummary":"Mazzuma, a Ghana-based startup, is working to provide greater access to artificial intelligence (AI) and blockchain technology. “We want to use our generative AI project to democratize AI—giving access to people who do not have the kind of expertise or research background to build language models at scale,” says Nii Osae, cofounder and director of software engineering at Mazzuma.\n\nThe company built a generative AI app, MazzumaGPT, using Amazon Web Services (AWS) and Amazon SageMaker—a service to build, train, and deploy machine learning (ML) models for virtually any use case with fully managed infrastructure, tools, and workflows. By using AWS, Mazzuma created this tool in months at low cost, and MazzumaGPT is now serving developers in 85 countries around the world.","imageSrcUrl":"https://d1.awsstatic.com/Customer%20References%20Directory%20Logos/mazzuma-logo%401x.8a32abe19c6b64e73f55fd1a7ff33b5dde0b70be.png","displayLocation":"Ghana","customerNameLower":"mazzuma","footerInfoText":"Published Date","industry":"Financial Services","sortDate":"2024-09-06","headlineUrl":"https://aws.amazon.com/solutions/case-studies/mazzuma/?did\u003dcr_card\u0026trk\u003dcr_card","customer-name":"Mazzuma","publishedDate":"2024","enableShare":"1","headline":"Mazzuma Reduces Training Time from 23 Hours to 30 Minutes Using DeepSpeed ZeRO on Amazon SageMaker","content